<% @title = 'House rules' %>

<%= render partial: 'sidebar' %>

<div id="left_column_flip" class="left_column_flip">
  <h1>
    <%= @title %>
  </h1>

  <p>
    If you break any of these rules, we may suspend your account. This means
    you won't be able to make requests or updates on WhatDoTheyKnow.
  </p>

  <p>
    When rules are broken, our volunteers have to spend a lot of time fixing
    things. This could make it harder for mySociety to keep running this
    service.
  </p>

  <%= render partial: 'help/house_rules/list_of_house_rules' %>

  <p>
    If you break these rules, you could be banned from the site. We may also
    remove your requests or annotations.
  </p>

  <p>
    We will usually contact you first and explain how to use the service
    properly, but we may act straight away if the behaviour is clearly malicious
    or there has been serious or repeated misuse.
  </p>

  <p>
    Our <a href="https://www.mysociety.org/code-of-conduct/">Code of
    Conduct</a> applies to all interactions with our team. If you use
    threatening, abusive or harassing language towards our staff or volunteers,
    we may stop responding to you and ban you from using the site. In serious
    cases, we may also report the matter to the police.
  </p>

  <%= render partial: 'history' %>

  <div id="hash_link_padding"></div>
</div>
